WEBVTT

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.690
Two dine on sticks... Five thirsty...

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.200
Five thirsty...

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.700
Two dine on sticks...

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.660
There you are, Kirin!

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.870
Two-nine-six! That's your number!

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.080
Five thirsty! There'll be five thirsty for sure!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.710
Five thirty...

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.010
Yay!

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.760
We both made it!

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.510
I passed, Akira!

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.890
Yep, Kirin did too.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.270
Thanks.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.270
Since you passed, will you be moving here?

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:51.070
Someplace close to Machiko, maybe?

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:53.030
I'm moving in with her, in fact.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.450
Rent in Tokyo's pretty expensive,

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:59.410
so I think it makes more sense to split it.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.960
Talk to you later.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.160
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.920
Hey, look!

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.510
The cherry trees are blossoming.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:14.880
Yeah.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.010
Hey, Ms. Uchiki.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.300
Did you already speak with the vice-principal?

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.510
Y-Yeah.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.100
<i>A new season is beginning.</i>

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.530
Father, Mother...

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.370
I'm going to Tokyo.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:09.540
Thank you for everything you've done for me.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.460
You don't need to get that
formal about it, Kirin.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.540
A-And <i>you</i>—

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:17.460
If only I had objected more strongly...

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:23.720
Now you'll go to college in Tokyo, find a job there, and even if you get married...

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:28.220
Wait, <i>I</i> was the one who was against her going to art school.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.850
You were on her side.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.600
Well, yes, but...

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.480
Dad...

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.740
Don't worry! I'll come back often!

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.740
I'll be here for planting, and for harvest!

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.910
Promise me, Kirin!

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.530
Jeez...

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.010
Today's the day I say goodbye to this uniform.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:07.010
It used to hang so loose on me, but now it fits perfectly—

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:15.520
I'm not putting on weight... am I?

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.280
Grandma, today's my middle school graduation.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.660
I'm on my way.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.790
<i>Graduation.</i>

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.920
<i>My last day of middle school.</i>

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.380
<i>The last day I'll walk through the gate.</i>

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.590
Machiko!

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:40.130
Morning.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.550
See you there!

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:42.800
Sure.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.510
<i>The last day I'll walk down these halls.</i>

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.310
<i>The last day I'll see everyone regularly.</i>

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.430
Yay!

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.150
Be seated.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.320
<i>There are so many parents here behind us.</i>

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.740
You're not supposed to cry yet, Hina.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.160
I know, but...

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:23.130
<i>Grandma came for my entrance ceremony.</i>

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.930
<i>I can't believe it's already been three years.</i>

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:31.680
<i>The meal she cooked to celebrate was so delicious...</i>

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.400
<i>I can't let my tummy rumble!</i>

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.200
<i>Let's pretend we didn't hear that.</i>

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.200
We will now present diplomas.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.910
<i>It feels like the entrance ceremony was just yesterday.</i>

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.870
Machiko Ryo.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:57.920
Yes!

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:04.800
<i>I almost feel like if I turn around, I'll see Grandma right there.</i>

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.760
<i>Kirin?!</i>

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.470
I thought you said you couldn't make it until after lunch.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.730
You surprised me!

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.770
I wanted to see your school at least once.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:25.230
Plus, my graduation was two days ago.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.990
I'm glad you didn't get lost on your way here.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.700
Well, I <i>am</i> a high school student now.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:36.000
I had a hard time getting by the secretary, though.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.620
<i>You must be lost. You need to wait here until your mom comes.</i>

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:45.500
I'm glad you came, though.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.380
I was just thinking about Grandma.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.850
Thinking that I'd only ever see her again in my memories.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.890
It made me feel kind of lonely.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.390
Ryo...

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:06.940
But I guess this isn't the time to be dwelling on the past.

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.400
You held up well, Ryo.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:19.160
Especially with how loud your tummy was rumbling.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.380
You heard it from all the way back there?!

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.960
Oh, is that Morino?

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:27.590
They're from cram—

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:31.720
They made it into the same high school as us.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.760
You too, Morino? Great!

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:40.430
We were in different classes at cram school, but we'll be together in high school.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.230
Let's do great!

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.270
Y-Yeah...

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:47.980
See, you don't even have to worry about making friends.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.110
Yeah.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.000
We bought a lot.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:03.500
It's not like we have a graduation party for two every day.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.630
Is it too heavy for you with the condiments too?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:12.880
Nah, it's still lighter than what I brought with me—

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:17.300
Wait, my stuff's still in a coin locker at the station!

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:18.760
Shall we go pick it up together?

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.470
Nah, I'll be fine.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.440
I'll be right back, so just hang on.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:24.310
Kirin—

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:31.780
Oh, well. Guess I'll get started on dinner.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:32.820
A hand?!

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.580
Did I scare you, Ryo?

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:44.120
S-Sorry, Akira.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.540
You said you had work today, so...

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.750
Don't worry about it.

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.630
And I'm sorry I couldn't make it in time for your graduation.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.470
Come to think of it, where's Kirin?

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:59.470
Hm? Oh, she went to pick up her things from the station.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:02.180
You knew she was coming?

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.100
Well...

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.940
Ryo, I'm really sorry I've always been so busy at the worst possible times.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:16.700
Don't worry about it. You've always been there when I needed a guardian's signature or something.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:21.540
You're like a second mother to me.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.210
You really are such a good girl!

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.420
And good girls deserve rewards!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.210
You don't need to make that an excuse to grope me!

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.720
Here you go.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.680
Thank you. Can I open it now?

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.720
Of course!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.930
An... apron?

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.650
It smells like Grandma.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:54.530
Mom made it out of her own apron.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:10:00.030
Two years ago, she told me to give it to you when you graduated.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.830
Two years ago?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:03.790
Yeah.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.000
Grandma...

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:12.920
<i>My room is a disaster zone, so I'm just glad I was able to find it!</i>

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:17.050
But why did she ask you?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.680
I said the same thing.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:22.100
Why? Can't you just give it to her yourself?

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.640
Don't say that.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:29.100
I might forget, so you should keep it.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:36.360
Neither of us really wanted to say it,
but she may have known what was coming.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.950
Anyway, I need to get back to work.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:47.370
See you!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.810
<i>Grandma's apron...</i>

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:13.360
<i>I want the first meal I cook while wearing Grandma's apron to be something special.</i>

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.980
I can still smell her.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.240
<i>It's reassuring.</i>

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:25.740
<i>It's as though she's here in the kitchen with me, just like old days.</i>

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:33.250
<i>She wore this apron while cooking for me.</i>

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:36.750
All right!

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:42.590
I'll recreate the meal she cooked to celebrate my getting into middle school!

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:47.260
Sashimi, fried chicken wings, and...

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:51.140
Her specialty, yellowtail and radish!

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:54.650
<i>I haven't made yellowtail and radish in a long time.</i>

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.780
<i>The last time was...</i>

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:05.660
It's not tasty at all!

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:09.910
It smells so good, but why does it taste so bad?

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:16.630
<i>I think I've gotten a bit better at cooking since then.</i>

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.590
The yellowtail and radish is done!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.590
I should give it a try first.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.600
Here goes.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.480
It's good.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:42.110
But it's still not quite the same as Grandma's.

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:47.200
There's still something missing, just like last time.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:53.540
<i>And it seems like I'm not that interested in eating it myself.</i>

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.540
<i>This is...</i>

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:03.670
Wow, it smells great in here! What is it?
What are you making?!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.550
Sorry it took so long.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.180
My stuff's pretty heavy, and I stopped at the market for a few things.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.940
Is that a mountaineering backpack?

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:18.060
And you brought a pillow, too?

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.110
Long story. I'll tell you later.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.400
Oh, you made yellowtail and radish?

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.490
It looks great! Can I have some?

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:27.610
Yes, of course.

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:45.630
Wow! It's meaty like a steak, but in its own way!

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.270
And the radish has soaked up so much of the rich yellowtail flavor!

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:11.780
That intense spark of spice, wrapped up in sweetness...

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.330
I could have bowl after bowl of rice with this.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:19.540
I could eat this with a mountain of rice the size of Fuji!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.540
Let's march on up!

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.170
W-Well...

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:24.920
I can't stop myself!

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.010
You know, it's true.

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:33.350
It tastes completely different than when I tried it before.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.680
It's far more satisfying, too.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:44.190
<i>Now that I have someone to eat it with...</i>

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.190
<i>This is the first time it's really tasted like Grandma's.</i>

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:51.200
I feel so good.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.950
Ryo, your stews are one-of-a-kind.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:56.370
That was great!

00:14:56.750 --> 00:15:00.120
It was Grandma's specialty.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:04.630
Is that apron her graduation gift to you?

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:10.090
I figured. It looks great on you.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.140
See? You can still make new memories with her.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.850
With Grandma?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:22.560
Yeah. Isn't wearing it while you cook her recipes a new memory?

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:29.650
I mean, memories are something you can look back on,
but they're also things you can make anew.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:36.490
That's wonderful, Kirin! You sound so grown-up.

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:40.870
Well, of course. I'm not a kid anymore.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.960
That was a really good line, right? Wasn't it?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:54.090
<i>Thank you for the wonderful present, Grandma.</i>

00:15:54.550 --> 00:16:01.350
<i>I never thought I'd still be able to make new memories with you.</i>

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:03.350
<i>I'm so happy right now.</i>

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:11.990
I won't dwell on the past anymore.

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:16.780
I have this apron. I have great friends.
I can move forward.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.790
Let's cook plenty of wonderful things together.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:27.920
Kirin, I'm counting on you too.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:35.220
I could eat my way around the world with your cooking.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:48.940
So you're moving today?

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.650
I guess you did bring a lot.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.490
Yeah. The movers should arrive soon.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.410
We'd better get going, then.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:59.330
We need to get you ready and head to your new place.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.500
Actually, wait, you already found somewhere?

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.580
Hm?

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.830
Yeah, here.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:10.340
I already had Akira take care of all the paperwork.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.930
"Here"? What do you mean?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:16.930
Huh?

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.010
Huh?!

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.270
What's this all about, Kirin?

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:27.520
I-I'm sorry. I thought Akira told you.

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:30.730
In fact, I thought <i>I</i> told you.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:34.070
That's probably the movers.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:35.700
Hi!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.240
Huh? The movers aren't here yet?

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.080
Even you knew, Shiina?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:43.950
Oh, man.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:49.460
Tsuyuko thought you'd be too busy with the move to cook.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.210
Here, shrimp cutlet sandwiches.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.930
Shrimp cutlet?

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.850
Yeah. The pork cutlets gave you luck on your exams,

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:08.100
so these should give you luck every day.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:09.980
That's pretty cool!

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.320
Um...

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.110
Mom? Dad?

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.410
We're here, Kirin!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:26.040
The co-op has the day off anyway,
so we thought we'd help you move.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:32.380
I suppose it makes sense that your parents would know too.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.590
Oh, you're all here!

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:35.460
Akira!

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:39.680
I managed to get the day off,
so I'll help out with the move...

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:40.220
Eh?

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.890
Ehhhh?

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.390
We're sorry!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:49.480
I can't believe everyone knew but me.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:55.820
I'm sorry! I got so caught up with the apron that I completely forgot to—

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.320
But I'm happy, too.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:03.240
I'm glad I get to live with Kirin.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.630
I'm so happy, Ryo!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:18.760
I don't know what I would have done if I couldn't move in with you!

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:23.800
You're just as forgetful as she is, Akira.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:27.270
It's all right.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:29.270
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:07.720
<i>When you left, I was all alone here,</i>

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:11.560
<i>but today, the place is full of people.</i>

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:25.700
Many hands make light work, huh?

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.200
Well, then...

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.580
Let's make something to eat!

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:31.370
Really?

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:46.720
So this is the legendary veggie stir-fry!

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.430
Dig in.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:50.930
All right.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.940
Let's eat!

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.450
Every day!

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:19.750
Oh, right, we should invite Yuki from downstairs as well.

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.710
I'll come too!

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:27.220
<i>I want to make lots more food with Grandma's apron.</i>

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.220
I hope she's home.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:32.350
Kirin.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:37.190
I'm looking forward to living with you.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.020
I'm looking forward to living with you too!

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.210
<i>We'll make lots of food.</i>

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.920
<i>And lots of memories.</i>

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:08.720
<i>Happy cooking, and happy memories.</i>
